## 8. EC2 IAM Role and S3 Integration

The EC2 instance uses an instance profile and IAM role to access S3. Long-term access keys are not required on the EC2 instance.

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| IAM Role | `CloudLab-EC2-S3-Role` |
| Instance Profile | `CloudLab-EC2-S3-Role` |
| Attached Policy | `CloudLab-S3-Backup-Policy` |
| S3 Bucket | `secure-cloud-backup-system24` |
| S3 Bucket Region | `ap-south-1` |
| Allowed object prefix | `ec2-backups/*` |

The policy configured for the lab grants object upload and download only in the project prefix. It also scopes bucket listing to the requested prefix:

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:GetObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::secure-cloud-backup-system24/ec2-backups/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:ListBucket",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::secure-cloud-backup-system24",
      "Condition": {
        "StringLike": {
          "s3:prefix": [
            "ec2-backups",
            "ec2-backups/*"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

S3 project path:

```text
s3://secure-cloud-backup-system24/ec2-backups/
```

Example commands (replace the placeholders with a real local file and object key):

```bash
# List the permitted project prefix
aws s3 ls s3://secure-cloud-backup-system24/ec2-backups/

# Upload an object
aws s3 cp <local-file> s3://secure-cloud-backup-system24/ec2-backups/<file-name>

# Download an object
aws s3 cp s3://secure-cloud-backup-system24/ec2-backups/<file-name> .
```

The lab upload and download test was successful, and the downloaded test file content was checked. Keep the IAM policy limited to the project bucket and prefix; do not grant broad `s3:*` permissions.

