| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| CloudWatch Region | `eu-north-1` |
| Dashboard | `CloudLab-monitoring24` |
| Alarm | `CloudLab-High-CPU-Alarm` |
| Namespace | `AWS/EC2` |
| Metric | `CPUUtilization` |
| Statistic | Average |
| Period | 5 minutes |
| Threshold | Greater than `80%` |
| Evaluation | 1 datapoint within 5 minutes |

The CloudWatch dashboard displays the EC2 CPU utilization metric. The alarm evaluates the average CPU utilization and enters the alarm state when the configured threshold condition is met.

The alarm was observed in **OK** state during the console review. That means CPU utilization was not breaching the configured threshold at that time; it does not mean the alarm is inactive.

